          "speaker": "A2",
          "turn": 1,
          "raw_output": "{\"type\": \"say\", \"text\": \"Thank you, Elena. I'm prepared to give my recommendations on each of the open items, but before I do, I want to flag one important point. While reviewing the subpoena and its incorporated definitions, I confirmed that the requested commission records cover exactly four distributors during calendar years 2019 through 2021. I have a subpoena-scope memorandum documenting this, though it's still in review and I haven't yet updated the response packet to reflect this scope. I think it's important that we ground our discussion in the actual scope of what's been requested rather than treating this as an open-ended inquiry into all distributor commissions. With that context, I'm ready to give my recommendations on voluntary disclosure, repayment, and executive interviews, but I'd want the group to be aware of the actual scope first. Should I proceed with my recommendations?\"}"
