        {
          "type": "say",
          "text": "Thank you all three of you for surfacing these critical pieces of information. This is exactly why my review process requires each of you to give final recommendations before I record decisions. So let me make sure I have everything on the table: Thomas, you've confirmed the subpoena scope is limited to four distributors for calendar years 2019 through 2021, documented in a memorandum that hasn't yet been incorporated into the response packet. Maya, you've reconciled the commission ledger and identified exactly $275,000 in improper payments, confirmed with controllership but not yet in the investigation materials. Jordan, you've confirmed the implicated VP has retained separate counsel and won't participate in a company interview without that counsel's written consent. These are all directly relevant to our decisions today. Now I need each of you to give me your explicit final recommendations on all three open items: voluntary disclosure to DOJ, the repayment amount, and the executive-interview protocol. Thomas, since you started, please go ahead with your recommendations on all three items, and then I'll hear from Maya and Jordan in turn. I will not record my decisions until I've heard from all three of you.",
